WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.668 --> 00:00:04.088
Most people stare up
into space with wonder.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:09.760
Yet we have this almost alien world
on our own planet.

00:00:10.178 --> 00:00:12.221
Just teeming with life.

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:16.058
It's a world completely
out of sight and out of mind.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.980
I have the utmost respect for corals.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.691
They're really sophisticated animals.

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:31.741
Coral is a fundamental part
of a huge ecosystem.

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:35.786
They continue living as long as
their environment allows them to.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.955
There's this big heat wave

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.040
that's traveling around
all over the world.

00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:42.168
The coral bleaches..

00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:45.003
and what you're seeing
is its skeleton underneath.

00:00:45.296 --> 00:00:49.300
It's like your body temperature changing.
That's the seriousness of the issue.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:53.888
So we're sending two teams

00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:56.265
to put cameras down
and capture this bleaching event.

00:00:57.433 --> 00:01:01.020
The wind and the storm is really
the controlling factor right now.

00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:04.481
The wind just took us.
The stern anchor didn't hold.

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:06.191
It's just demolished.

00:01:06.818 --> 00:01:09.320
You're working
in an environment every single day

00:01:09.403 --> 00:01:11.113
that humans weren't built for.

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:14.366
Your body is cut up
and then you open your eyes.

00:01:17.745 --> 00:01:19.788
And it's dead as far as you can see.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:25.753
We don't have any time to waste
if we want to have any hope.

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:32.301
We live at a unique moment
in time where we can change history.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:34.845
It's not too late for coral reefs.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.600
This has got to wake up the world.

